WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it. Let's
make sure you pass.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Refrigerant safety: liquid refrigerant causes frostbite on skin contact.
Refrigerant vapor is heavier than air and displaces oxygen in enclosed spaces
causing asphyxiation. Decomposed refrigerant (from flame contact) produces

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Phosgene: Toxic gas produced when refrigerant contacts an open flame. Extremely
dangerous.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Asphyxiation: Suffocation from oxygen displacement. Refrigerant vapor sinks and
displaces breathable air.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Refrigerant safety is tested on every EPA
608 section. More importantly it keeps you alive.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Refrigerant is heavier than air and sinks. And — Never use
open flame leak detectors

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Quick check: what is the maximum fine for knowingly venting refrigerant? If you
don't know that number, go back and read it again.

